---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Who's Most Likely To?"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Who's Most Likely To? Android app developed by Jacob."
>
  <section class="pt-28 pb-16 md:pt-32 md:pb-24">
    <div class="container-app max-w-3xl">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 hover:text-accent-600 dark:hover:text-accent-400 transition-colors mb-8"
      >
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to portfolio
      </a>

      <span class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase notranslate">
        Legal
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 mb-4">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2">
        <span class="notranslate">Who's Most Likely To?</span>
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-500 notranslate">
        Last updated: July 3, 2026
      </p>

      <div class="prose-policy mt-10 space-y-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy describes how <span class="notranslate">Jacob</span>
          ("the developer", "we", "us") handles information in connection with the
          <span class="notranslate">Who's Most Likely To?</span> Android application
          ("the App"). We have written it in plain language so you can quickly
          understand what we do and do not do with your data.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 notranslate">
            1. Data we do NOT collect
          </h2>
          <p>
            The App does not require an account, does not ask for an email address,
            does not request your real name, and does not collect any content you
            create. All gameplay data — questions, settings, and your local
            statistics — is stored exclusively on your device and is not sent to
            our servers (we do not operate any servers for this App).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 notranslate">
            2. Data that IS processed (through Google AdMob)
          </h2>
          <p>
            To keep the App free, we display advertising served by
            <span class="notranslate">Google AdMob</span>
            (<span class="notranslate">Google Ireland Ltd.</span>). AdMob may
            process the following information from your device in order to
            deliver ads and measure their performance:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Google Advertising ID (GAID).</li>
            <li>Coarse IP address (truncated by Google).</li>
            <li>Device and app information (model, OS version, app version).</li>
            <li>Ad interaction events (impressions, clicks, video views).</li>
            <li>Banner-format advertising shown within the App (Google AdMob banner units).</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can read more about how Google uses data from partner sites
            and apps
            <a
              href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
              class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              target="_blank">here</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can reset or delete your Advertising ID at any time from your
            device's settings: <em>Settings &rarr; Google &rarr; Ads</em>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 notranslate">
            3. EEA, UK and Switzerland consent
          </h2>
          <p>
            If you are located in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom
            or Switzerland, the App will show a consent form (Google's User
            Messaging Platform, "UMP") the first time you open it. You can
            accept, reject, or change your choice at any time from your
            device's Google settings. We do not serve personalised advertising
            to users who have not granted consent.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 notranslate">
            4. Children
          </h2>
          <p>
            The App is not directed at children under 13 years of age. The
            "Spicy" question category, which is intended for adult audiences,
            is protected by an in-app age gate that requires the user to
            confirm they are 18 or older before any of its content is shown.
            We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you are a parent or guardian and believe a child has provided
            personal information through the App, please contact us using the
            email address below so we can assist you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 notranslate">
            5. In-app purchases and payments
          </h2>
          <p>
            The current version of the App is entirely free and does not
            contain any in-app purchases, subscriptions, or paid features.
            If this changes in a future version, this section will be updated
            before the change is released.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 notranslate">
            6. Data retention
          </h2>
          <p>
            Because we do not collect personal data on our servers, we do not
            retain any of it. Local data stored on your device (settings,
            scores, remembered player names) can be erased at any time from
            the App's <em>Settings</em> screen, or by uninstalling the App.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 notranslate">
            7. Your rights
          </h2>
          <p>
            Depending on where you live, you may have rights under laws such
            as the GDPR (EU/EEA), the UK GDPR, the CCPA/CPRA (California), or
            the LGPD (Brazil). These rights may include the right to access,
            correct, delete, or port your data. Because we do not hold your
            data on our servers, fulfilling most of these rights can be done
            directly inside the App or by uninstalling it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 notranslate">
            8. Changes to this policy
          </h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy to reflect legal, technical, or business
            changes. The most current version will always be available at this
            URL, and the "Last updated" date at the top of the page will be
            revised accordingly. If a change is material, we will display a
            notice inside the App before it takes effect.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 notranslate">
            9. Contact
          </h2>
          <p>
            For any question, request, or complaint regarding this Privacy
            Policy or the way the App handles information, please contact:
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            <a
              href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline font-medium notranslate"
            >
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" />
              </svg>
              kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com
            </a>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-500">
            We aim to respond to all privacy-related enquiries within 30 days.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
